> of strength used on this kind of sling like a bow or crossbow.

I'm pretty sure the David vs Goliath sling is the kind that's in
Nethack, it seems to be the kind depicted in the graphic for the
weapon.

Anyway, I think this is an excellent idea!  It helps to differentiate
the weapons a bit more, it gives some players (high strength ones) more
of a reason to go with slings over bows (slings are a bit useless since
the ammo weighs so much and they do less damage than bows, although
that's somewhat balanced by the fact that ammo is so common), and the
critical hit idea is cool as well.  It even makes Hobbits more
interesting to play!

Suggestions:
1. Strength penalties should be factored in as well.  If you can't get
a good swing behind the stone, of course, it isn't going to hurt much.
2. The critical hit idea, if it's an instant kill, is too powerful.
That should be changed to a knock-unconscious (or at least stunning)
effect, also be dependent on the user's dexterity (since only head hits
will do this), be useless against headless monsters, and also be
dependent on the monster being large-size or bigger (as Goliath, heh).
Monsters with tough skin (anything a bullwhip won't hurt) should be
harder to stun like this.

